            "bug_id": 19143,
            "text": "Unfortunately, unlike the second half of your example in comment 4, a `CE_UTF8` string comes out of `translateChar()` with `C` locale in place containing the replacement sequence `<U+00E5>`, not the desired `0xe5` byte. It might be that `_wsetlocale` is the only solution that doesn't rely on undocumented behaviour (UCRT assigning meaning to bytes outside ASCII in the `C` locale).",
